Portage 3.0.83 resolver patches, re-cut into independent sub-series (2026-11-21)
================================================================================

This directory holds the ladder of sys-apps/portage::pwr (formerly 25 patches) cut again
into 30 patches that form 13 sub-series, A to M. Every line of code is the same as before:

  * all 30 files applied in numeric order to pristine 3.0.83 (patch -p1 -F0) give the tested
    tree, byte for byte, and so do the first 1, 3, 9, 11, 14, 16 and 18 of them compared with
    the same prefixes of the 25-patch ladder (0001-0018 are the same changes as before; only
    their context lines differ);
  * every sub-series applies alone, in its own order, to pristine 3.0.83 without any patch of
    another sub-series, byte-compiles, and gives the same merge list in the same order with the
    same number of backtracking attempts and packages as unpatched 3.0.83 on the six test states;
  * any two sub-series apply together in numeric order (78 pairs tried, no textual conflict),
    and so does the series with any one sub-series left out.

Every patch header carries a line "Sub-series: <letter> (<name>) - patch <i> of <n>; ...".
To use one sub-series, apply its files in numeric order:

    for n in 0009 0019; do patch -p1 -F0 < $n-*.patch; done      # sub-series D

patch reports offsets (line numbers are those of the full series); with -F0 it uses no fuzz.


Sub-series
----------

"Alone on stock" = resolve seconds of `emerge -p -uND @world`, summed over the six states
(start holds masks py313 bdeps policykit), ONE run per state, with only this sub-series on
stock 3.0.83; the stock arm was run in the same pass. Gate ok = on all six states the merge list
in order, the backtracking attempts and the package count equal the stock arm. The figures are
single runs: differences of a few seconds between arms are inside the noise.

A  probe, match and config memos
     0001 probe-memo
     0002 match-replay
     0004 probe-upgrade-downgrade-memo
     0005 probe-similar-lazy-replay
     0012 regenerate-memos
     0013 probe-memo-object
     0014 probe-version-bounds
     0016 pkg-use-without-setcpv
     0028 atom-key-caches
     0029 probe-certain-atoms
     Memos for the slot-operator probes inside one _slot_operator_trigger_reinstalls loop,
     replay of atom matches across backtracking attempts, memos for config.regenerate() and
     package USE without setcpv(); on top of these the probes pass over versions that cannot
     qualify and atoms that dep_check() cannot drop.
     Alone on stock: 256.6 s against stock 447.3 s (-43 %), gate ok

B  cycle search and frontier
     0003 mergeable-from-frontier
     0006 empty-cycle-search-memo
     0007 one-node-cycle-shortcut
     0010 frontier-leaf-sets
     0011 gather-ok-tracker
     0024 frontier-mergeable-set-node-removal
     The selection loop of _serialize_tasks takes mergeable nodes and cycle-search state
     from the leaf frontier: exact leaf sets, no repeated search that found no cycle, one-
     node closures, a tracker that skips the cycle-closure pass.
     Alone on stock: 375.3 s against stock 447.3 s (-16 %), gate ok

C  use_reduce parser
     0008 use-reduce-store
     0018 c-parser-atom-memo
     0030 use-reduce-store-rewrap
     use_reduce(): parse results kept beyond the 1,024-entry LRU, an atom memo in the C
     parser glue, the C parser also for calls with is_valid_flag.
     Alone on stock: 407.1 s against stock 447.3 s (-9 %), gate ok

D  garbage collector
     0009 gc-threshold
     0019 pretend-gc-off-fast-exit
     Cyclic garbage collector: higher threshold during the resolve; for `emerge --pretend`
     no collection during the run and os._exit instead of heap teardown.
     Alone on stock: 420.2 s against stock 447.3 s (-6 %), gate ok

E  single-atom lookups
     0015 single-atom-lookups
     Matches one atom against one package directly, without building a package set.
     Alone on stock: 399.6 s against stock 447.3 s (-11 %), gate ok

F  slot-object constructors
     0017 slot-object-constructors
     SlotObject sets ordinary slots directly; explicit constructors for Dependency and
     _dep_choice.
     Alone on stock: 427.5 s against stock 447.3 s (-4 %), gate ok

G  flat dependency lists
     0020 flat-dep-lists
     Builds the dep_check() result directly for dependency lists that contain no choice.
     Alone on stock: 434.9 s against stock 447.3 s (-3 %), gate ok

H  atom matching caches
     0021 atom-matching-caches
     One-atom path in match_from_list(), slot descriptors for Atom attributes, unbounded
     vercmp/catpkgsplit caches.
     Alone on stock: 430.8 s against stock 447.3 s (-4 %), gate ok

I  REQUIRED_USE memo
     0022 required-use-memo
     Remembers per (package, enabled USE) whether REQUIRED_USE is satisfied, for all
     backtracking attempts.
     Alone on stock: 443.1 s against stock 447.3 s (-1 %), gate ok

J  priority copy
     0023 priority-copy
     Copies dependency priorities slot by slot and builds them from templates.
     Alone on stock: 439.6 s against stock 447.3 s (-2 %), gate ok

K  config trims
     0025 config-trims
     Small memos in the per-package config work (USE mask/force stacks, ACCEPT_LICENSE
     stack, config._getitem, the RESTRICT/PROPERTIES USE set).
     Alone on stock: 434.6 s against stock 447.3 s (-3 %), gate ok

L  flatten-atoms memo
     0026 flatten-atoms-memo
     Moves the _flatten_atoms() cache to _frozen_config so that backtracking attempts share
     it.
     Alone on stock: 439.2 s against stock 447.3 s (-2 %), gate ok

M  leftovers
     0027 leftovers
     Six local rewrites of hot statements (Package.__bool__, metadata wrapper constructor,
     digraph.add, dep_expand, noise-level tests in dep_check, _pkg_use_enabled).
     Alone on stock: 434.9 s against stock 447.3 s (-3 %), gate ok

